<!-- The paddle glows on its own, wherever it is.

     What decides whether something blooms is its emissive colour **in linear space** times
     `emissiveIntensity`, against the `<Bloom threshold>`. #0d9488 at 1.1 came to 0.33 with the
     threshold at 1, so the paddle never glowed by itself — it only lit up when it drove through
     the warm light that used to sit at the centre of the field. A brighter teal at 1.3 comes to
     0.86: over the threshold, so it glows at both ends of its travel, and under white, so the
     surface keeps its colour instead of clipping. -->
<MeshStandardMaterial color="#5eead4" emissive="#2dd4bf" emissiveIntensity="1.3"
                      roughness="0.2" metalness="0.5" />
